{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1003192-skin-dancer-questions","id":1003192,"title":"Skin Dancer Questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-14T18:52:23-08:00","id":1003192,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Skin Dancer Questions","content":"Ok So i am new to the the Skin Dancers and i just want to get my fact straight.<br /> <br /> Any Kinfolk can become a Skin Dancer? Does that work with changing breeds too?<br /> Can Skin Dancers count as a Shiftier after the right or a Kinfolk when it comes to breeding?<br /> <br /> Could a Skin Dancer gain pelts from willing subjects (no Wyrm Taint chance) who may be only found in the deep umbra and if being a kinfolk of those breeds help bring back some of the lost Breeds?<br /> <br /> I am just trying to work out the impossible parts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Like the Sun I am relentless even in death...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3293-rahod","name":"Rahod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T21:10:35-08:00","id":1003230,"title":"","content":"Yes, other changing breeds can use similar rites. My understanding is they will count as their respective breed for breeding purposes, not kinfolk.<br /> <br /> As for extinct breeds, I doubt it, but only because after a long time garou and fera become spirits and lose their physical form. It would thus be difficult to find enough skins of those breeds without time travel, and there's also the issue of reconnecting with their various totems and patron spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T21:34:13-08:00","id":1003238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1003192-skin-dancer-questions#post1003192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Any Kinfolk can become a Skin Dancer? Does that work with changing breeds too?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably. I don't believe it's come up. There is a chance they would need a different Rite, which I say based solely on how magic tends to work in the WoD.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1003192-skin-dancer-questions#post1003192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Can Skin Dancers count as a Shiftier after the right or a Kinfolk when it comes to breeding?</div> </div> </div> </div>They should breed true. They are shifters for all intents from the completion of the Ritual forward.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1003192-skin-dancer-questions#post1003192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Could a Skin Dancer gain pelts from willing subjects (no Wyrm Taint chance) who may be only found in the deep umbra and if being a kinfolk of those breeds help bring back some of the lost Breeds?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes to the first part, they could theoretically get the pelts from willing subjects, though there is argument the Ritual itself is Wyrm tainted. Also, for clarification, by &quot;willing&quot; do you mean donated upon death, or actually skinning the shifter alive?<br /> second and third parts: Deep Umbra denizens tend not to be shifters anymore (as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5307_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5307\" data-vbnamecard=\"5307\">loomer</a>mentioned) due to disconnection. And the extinct breeds don't have kinfolk anymore which would put a dent in the plan to start.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T21:48:57-08:00","id":1003244,"title":"","content":"Any kinfolk can theoretically become a Skin Dancer.<br /> <br /> The Rite doesn't work for other Fera, but nothing explicitly states that the kin of other Fera couldn't go down the same path and find their own version if you want that.<br /> <br /> It's possible that you could get willing pelts, but it finding five people willing to die for you is kinda hard, and you still have to appeal to banes to empower the Rite.<br /> <br /> Using it to bring back the lost Breeds wouldn't really work logistically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T00:24:29-08:00","id":1003268,"title":"","content":"I'm kinda gonna go against the grain on this one. You can actually skin spirits, sort of. Rite of the Flayed God from BotW involves making spirits into cloaks or clothing via harvesting their hollow 'shells.' Additionally, some spirits expressly have something akin to a physicality, depending on their native realm. Places like Pangea or Arcadia have spirits that behave like animals and people, according to my ancient copy of the Umbra book... which means they got skins to take, if you got a way to keep ahold of it once you leave the realm.<br /> <br /> Of course, Rite of the Flayed God is torturous and Wyrmish, and you have to be a changing breed to enact it in the first place, so it doesn't mean that exact rite is the solution to your problem, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3293-rahod\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3293\" data-vbnamecard=\"3293\">Rahod</a>, but it still means an enterprising and mystically inclined being could liberate a spirit's epidermis; it isn't impossible, clearly.<br /> <br /> Since resurrecting dead breeds is pretty far off the rez anyway, why not come up with a 'skinning knife' fetish or tanning unguent talens that allow for specific types of ancestors to be skinned? You get a kinfolk with gnosis that could attune to the stuff, and then all they need is means of traveling to umbral realms, and then actually getting their hands on ancestors to flay. Succeed or fail, sounds like an interesting (and messy!) story.<br /> <br /> It seems more likely to result in some sort of botched mockery breed than anything else, but hey, if you want all the magical skullduggery to come to a happier conclusion in your story, be my guest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 11-15-2016, 03:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T01:09:47-08:00","id":1003281,"title":"","content":"First yes the rite of sacred rebirth works for any breed and kinfolk*<br /> <br /> Second short of a fetish and I could think of several spirits that might work, I would rule against skinning the spirits of Umbral ancient shapeshifters.<br /> <br /> Lastly, I could envision a kinfolk learning the rite then proceeding to gain the needed skins by killing BSD, but I would still rule the rite as tainted I would also think long and hard about allowing a player as a Skin Dancer no matter where or how they collected the skins. I think the Skin Dancer's while grounded in &quot;real world&quot; Werewolf lore are just a bit much at least for my campaigns to allow as player characters. I could see a few as NPC's perhaps not enemies or allies but somewhere in the zone of contacts that may or may not sell you down the river if the price where right.<br /> <br /> *Except Corax and Camazotz both breeds have a rite and no blood relationship is needed as far as I can tell. It seems to be tradition which tends to be stronger than the RULES.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T05:58:18-08:00","id":1004357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1003192-skin-dancer-questions#post1003192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any Kinfolk can become a Skin Dancer?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1003192-skin-dancer-questions#post1003192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does that work with changing breeds too?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. The rite was originally created by the Balam (per Shattered Dreams) and Haight simply tweaked the ritual to work for him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1003192-skin-dancer-questions#post1003192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Skin Dancers count as a Shiftier after the right or a Kinfolk when it comes to breeding?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think there has ever been any official ruling on this, so I would says its at Storyteller discretion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1003192-skin-dancer-questions#post1003192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could a Skin Dancer gain pelts from willing subjects (no Wyrm Taint chance) who may be only found in the deep umbra and if being a kinfolk of those breeds help bring back some of the lost Breeds?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and No. Kinfolk can only use the rite on lycans of their linage. Example, Samual Haight was a Garou Kinfolk so he could only enact the rite using Garou pelts (he actually tried using pelts from other Fera and it failed).<br /> <br /> The problem here becomes that even if the Kinfolk had linage back to the fallen breeds, by this time period it would most likely have been breed out of them. Most of the kinfolk were integrated into the other breeds 'pool' after a breed died out.<br /> <br /> If you get passed that then per the new changing breeds book it states that last remnants of most of the fallen breeds ran into umbra to hide from extinction. So, even though they are tied to the umbra now, I would say that if a kinfolk managed to find them; he or she could in fact theoretically do what you are saying.<br /> <br /> Not many survivors went into the umbra though. Its not like you could restart the breed given that it requires 5 pelts to use the rite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T06:53:46-08:00","id":1006684,"title":"","content":"Hello,<br /> <br /> In my perspective:<br /> <br /> 1) Yes, but just with the pelts corresponding with her breed. The W20 - Shattered Dreams clearly speaks about Aztec jaguar warrior skin dancers. The skinner himself also stole the Rite from Balam skindancers.<br /> <br /> 2) The rite itself answers this question: &quot;...allows to became a Garou...&quot; So she becames a werewolf with all of the merits and drawbacks.<br /> <br /> 3) The spirits in the deep umbra are spirits, and not changers. They seem to be the fallen breeds, they speak &amp; tase like them, and think like them. Maybe they don't even know they aren't Fera anymore. But they changed irreversibly. Their parts are become epheperma &amp; can't be a focus of this ritual, even if you could conserve them with other ones.<br /> <br /> Other books (Player's Guide, or Past Lifes maybe?) states, that:<br /> a) If your animal kin is extinct or tamed the Fera can't produce changer offsprings.<br /> b) In some cases (bats &amp; ravens) a totem's intervention is needed to form new &quot;offsprings&quot;. Bat is fallen. Rites won't work.<br /> <br /> Reviving a member of an dead tribe won't resurrect a tribe. A totem is also needed. A pure-breeded BSD Ronin, won't become White Howlers.<br /> <br /> Also the Rite won't work, because you, as was mentioned earlier, don't have Kinfolk of the lost. The changer &quot;genes&quot; / heritage dilutes after ~3 generations. (Shattered Dreams.) That's why we dont have kins of all Fera &amp; changer births are uncommon<br /> <br /> (Also you need 5 pelts harvested under the same auspice, which would be quite difficult.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T08:37:02-08:00","id":1006727,"title":"","content":"Minor niggle: Bat isn't wholly fallen. An Aspect of the Bat totem has been redeemed, which is why Bat spirits can teach the Garou gifts, act as pack totems, ect.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T10:15:14-08:00","id":1006758,"title":"","content":"Yep, I agree, but it's just a minor splinter of the whole, without it's full potential, so fallen from his power. (By the way, he was a little unhinged all the time.) His full (forced) recovery could be an epic quest (or the good use of Malleable Spirit).<br /> <br /> <br /> If somebody is realy intrested in bringing back the Lost Ones, there is an offician way to do it (, what I wouldn't allow). You need the access of a &quot;memory&quot; realm, an unique rite &amp; permission from Incarna Mnemosyne &amp; someone to be sacrificed willingly. You need to bind the deceased's spirit into the victim, make the hoodoovoodoo. The victim is lost, the Lost is reborn. (Shattered Dreams. - I think they've lost some of their pills, but it's one of the best W20 book so far.)<br /> (Still won't bring back a tribe or breed because the reasons above.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":562,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","user":"Lachdanan","date":". 11-22-2016, 01:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T12:17:01-08:00","id":1007796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1003192-skin-dancer-questions?p=1003230#post1003230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for extinct breeds, I doubt it, but only because after a long time garou and fera become spirits and lose their physical form. It would thus be difficult to find enough skins of those breeds without time travel, and there's also the issue of reconnecting with their various totems and patron spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about skins preserved in permafrost ?<br /> Jurassic Park like...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T19:11:19-08:00","id":1007906,"title":"","content":"The skin must be flayed from a living Fera, as memory serves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T21:20:16-08:00","id":1007937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1003192-skin-dancer-questions?p=1007906#post1007906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The skin must be flayed from a living Fera, as memory serves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah. I know they can be deceased since you can kill for them. They have to be specially preserved though I believe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T04:11:36-08:00","id":1010575,"title":"","content":"The rite itself is inherently deeply Wyrm tainted, so even if you do involve willing individuals you won't end up 100% right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T22:44:55-08:00","id":1010944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1003192-skin-dancer-questions?p=1010575#post1010575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rite itself is inherently deeply Wyrm tainted, so even if you do involve willing individuals you won't end up 100% right.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI'd say the version that Haight brought is inherently tainted, but the original probably wasn't.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe Balam probably thought it was fairly normal that if they were to die in battle, their skin would be used to bolster their number via worthy Kin. (Assuming they died in a manner which could be relatively quickly skinned.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T20:37:59-08:00","id":1011337,"title":"","content":"nevermind that their culture is different from that of garou and they likely viewed the ritual different from the (deeply christian paranoid acting) garou. The garou are supposed to be religious fanatics akin to jihadis in their zealotry for gaia. Isn't there a book coming out on that fairly soon?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T20:48:10-08:00","id":1011345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1003192-skin-dancer-questions?p=1011337#post1011337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">nevermind that their culture is different from that of garou and they likely viewed the ritual different from the (deeply christian paranoid acting) garou. The garou are supposed to be religious fanatics akin to jihadis in their zealotry for gaia. Isn't there a book coming out on that fairly soon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh, what? Jihadis are deluded and Werewolves are largely correct within the context of their own game. Not really that similar. It isn't a matter of believing in something that may or may not be true. Garou can see Gaia dying in the grip of the Wyrm... extremists that fly planes into buildings or hack up college kids with butcher knives aren't equivalent to the shapechanging protagonists of WtA.<br /> <br /> Edit: I mean, I get it, they both kill people in the name of pretend deities, but the setting of WtA also sort of hinges on the stuff that the Garou see in the umbra being more than halfway accurate. If the Wyrm isn't really bad or Gaia doesn't exist and all the blood the Garou spill is for nothing, then they are pretty similar, but that isn't the case unless you heavily edit your setting as a storyteller.<br /> <br /> 'Zeal' isn't inherently bad if you are zealous for a just cause.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 12-02-2016, 11:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T21:09:00-08:00","id":1011359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1003192-skin-dancer-questions?p=1011345#post1011345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Uh, what? Jihadis are deluded and Werewolves are largely correct within the context of their own game. Not really that similar. It isn't a matter of believing in something that may or may not be true. Garou can see Gaia dying in the grip of the Wyrm... extremists that fly planes into buildings or hack up college kids with butcher knives aren't equivalent to the shapechanging protagonists of WtA.<br /> <br /> Edit: I mean, I get it, they both kill people in the name of pretend deities, but the setting of WtA also sort of hinges on the stuff that the Garou see in the umbra being more than halfway accurate. If the Wyrm isn't really bad or Gaia doesn't exist and all the blood the Garou spill is for nothing, then they are pretty similar, but that isn't the case unless you heavily edit your setting as a storyteller.<br /> <br /> 'Zeal' isn't inherently bad if you are zealous for a just cause.</div> </div> </div> </div>unless the spirals have been right all along.<br /> <br /> One of the things that outlines the negative zealot nature of the garou is the second war of rage, specifically as outlined in shattered dreams. The balam wind em up screaming &quot;wyrm&quot; and just point them at the country side. Not something a rational or righteous individual/group does. <br /> <br /> The similarity to the jihadis is not so much the willing to fly airplanes into things, and more the willing to die with such fervent devotion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T00:25:03-08:00","id":1011401,"title":"","content":"Got a lot of thoughts on this so I am just gonna hold down the trigger and see what comes out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1003192-skin-dancer-questions?p=1011359#post1011359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">unless the spirals have been right all along.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok. But they aren't; they are insane and debauched and pathetic. Their own hubris led them into the Wyrm's coils and now they want to turn the planet into an ash heap. They are not wise or privy to some secret knowledge... they are wretched.<br /> <br /> And the Garou are far from perfect, but any war is going to be filled with grotesqery and tragedy. For all of their many, many flaws, the Garou and other Fera are still the good guys and gals fighting against an implacable and relentless evil.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1003192-skin-dancer-questions?p=1011359#post1011359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The similarity to the jihadis is not so much the willing to fly airplanes into things, and more the willing to die with such fervent devotion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, that just seems like a damn negative comparison. Dying for a cause is fine; it is motive that distinguishes between suicidal mass shooters and Alamo defenders. As far as zealotry goes, as a framework for a game featuring berserk warrior shapeshifters it is pretty useful. On some level, to have believable violent conflict you need a strong reason to put oneself in harm's way. WtA is great at giving werewolves a spiritual/cultural reason to war with the Wyrm. It is what the game is about. If you took away the animalistic bloodlust, the fanaticism, that gung-ho drive kill, it just wouldn't be Werewolf the Apocalypse.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}